WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.202
-House GOP leader Kevin McCarthy

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:05.838
threw a nearly nine-hour
tantrum on the House floor

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.774
as Democrats passed their
signature social spending bill.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.243
Meanwhile, one Republican
senator continued to spread

00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:13.079
Trump's big lie
about the election

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.282
and another accused a Biden
nominee of being a communist.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.951
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:23.156
♪♪

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.324
There was a temptation
during his presidency

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.360
to believe that Donald Trump
and the fringe movement

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.162
of goons and weirdos
who supported him

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.464
were not necessarily the core
of the modern GOP,

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.098
that once Trump
faded away,

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:35.568
the party would return
to some semblance of normalcy.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.638
But over and over, Republicans
keep proving how naive and wrong

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.505
that assumption was.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:40.639
And look, I get it.

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:42.308
I think lots of people
were hoping

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.809
this would be
a Beetlejuice situation

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.711
where we could just say
his name three times

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.414
and he would disappear
into that waiting room

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:50.116
where he'd finally look
like he fits in.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.452
"We love shrunken head guy,
don't we, folks?

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:55.454
We don't talk about him enough.
regularly about it.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.690
Love his tiny head.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.058
And of course, what a seat next

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.959
to the great Geena Davis,
League of Their Own'?

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:02.895
What a film. What a film.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.831
They say there's no crying
in baseball,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.133
but when Kit plowed into Dottie
and she dropped the ball,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.670
I'll admit I had a little bit
of dust in my eye."

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.872
Anyhow...

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.007
By the way, we're trying
a new transitional word today

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:16.442
instead of "anyway."

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.711
Are you delivering a comedic
digest of the day's news?

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.679
Did you get stuck
in a nonsensical tangent and

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:22.047
need a way back to the politics

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.883
but used "anyway"
too many times?

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.286
Try anyhow "anyhow."
[ Chime dings ]

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.087
Anyhow, Trump did not disappear,

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.089
and even if he did,
the brand of politics

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.825
he represented is very much
alive and well within the GOP

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.894
and not just among some
obscure lunatics in the House.

00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:39.165
Texas Senator Ted Cruz
was just on CBS this weekend,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.433
continuing to spread
the big lie

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.902
that there was widespread
fraud in the 2020 election

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.304
and defend his role in trying
to overturn the results

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.773
on January 6th.
-I brought together a group

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:49.209
of 11 senators,

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:53.245
and we objected to call for
a for an electoral commission

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.882
to review the claims of voter
fraud and to assess

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:58.117
and make a determination
to consider the evidence,

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.519
which I think would have been
much better for our democracy

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:04.123
because we right now have a
substantial chunk of our country

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:07.159
that has real doubts about
the integrity of the election.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.028
And if we had had
a credible electoral commission

00:02:10.028 --> 00:02:11.631
do an emergency audit,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.966
it would have enhanced
faith in democracy.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.702
But instead, Democrats
and a lot of the press

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:20.006
decided to just engage
in incendiary rhetoric

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.274
rather than acknowledge
voter fraud is real.

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:24.477
It is a problem...
-Well, do you have --

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.179
-...and the allegations
of voter fraud

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.147
needed to be examined
on the merits.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.149
-Alright, first of all,
over 60 cases

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.584
did examine the evidence,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.120
and not one found any merit
in any of Trump's claims.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.989
That includes judges
appointed by Trump

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.623
and the GOP-dominated
Supreme Court.

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.925
You think a judge appointed
by Trump himself

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.761
would turn down
the opportunity to help out?

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.030
They were probably getting
nonstop texts from him

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.266
begging for help
like an ex who won't go away.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.401
Seriously, did you forget
about all that?

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:50.369
I mean, how could you?

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:51.503
Rudy Giuliani is probably

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:53.339
still standing outside
the Supreme Court,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:56.109
banging on the front door
like a guy who just got evicted

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.110
from his apartment
for hoarding cats.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.547
"Hey, those aren't my pets.
Those are my law partners.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:02.881
You can't do this to

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:06.419
Whiskers, Whiskers,
Giuliani and Klein."

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.053
And look,
it's not like Republicans

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.522
stopped looking for voter fraud

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.291
after Biden's election
was certified.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.992
CNN reported back in October

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:16.128
that a week after the 2020
election, Texas Lt. Governor

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.997
Dan Patrick announced
that he was offering up

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.467
to $1 million to incentivize,
encourage, and reward people

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.436
to come forward
and report voter fraud.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.738
Nearly a year later,
Patrick, a Republican,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.173
has paid out his first reward

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.808
$25,000 to a Democrat
in Pennsylvania

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:33.446
who reported a Republican
who, after voting once,

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.415
attempted to vote
a second time as his son.

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:38.851
That's right,
Patrick had to pay the reward

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.019
to a registered Democrat
who reported a Republican

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:42.188
that was 72 years old

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.656
for trying to vote
a second time as a son.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.759
How does a 72-ear-old man
try and vote as his son?

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:50.630
Does he put on a dark baseball
hat and Ray Ban sunglasses?

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.498
I don't know. Let's take
a look at the article.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.368
Oh, that is what he did.
Alright.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.103
Probably made
a big show of it too.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.205
"Voting for squares like my dad.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.606
But for an election
this important,

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:04.343
I guess I can live
with being lame for once.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:07.479
Where's the nearest
skateboard park?

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:10.816
I'm 51."

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:12.718
Anyhow...
[ Chime dings ]

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:13.852
...the GOP is still

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:15.821
very much devoted to Trump
and his brand,

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.123
whether it's spreading
the big lie

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.858
that the 2020 election
was stolen

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.294
or embodying the ideology
and performance of Trumpism,

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.562
the unhinged
conspiracy mongering

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.331
and dark implications
of a hidden plot

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.100
or sinister enemies
around every corner.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.702
In fact, the GOP is so morally
and intellectually bankrupt,

00:04:30.702 --> 00:04:32.872
they've circled all the way back
to accusing people

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:35.808
of being secret communists,
Joe McCarthy style.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.142
-An outrageous turn during

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:39.945
an already contentious
confirmation hearing Thursday,

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.981
Republican Senator
John Kennedy of Louisiana

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.450
suggesting the nominee
who grew up in a country

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.452
that was still under
Soviet Union control

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.621
might still support
communist policy.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.890
Saule Omarova
is President Biden's pick

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.092
to be Comptroller
of the Currency.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.660
-I don't mean any disrespect.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:58.731
I don't know whether to call you
professor or comrade.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.700
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.801
-Senator...

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.305
...I'm not a communist.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:09.375
I do not subscribe
to that ideology.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.010
I could not choose
where I was born.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:16.215
My family suffered
under the communist regime.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.750
I came to this country.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.852
I'm proud to be an American,

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:22.055
and this is why
I'm here today, Senator.

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.356
-That's Louisiana
Senator John Kennedy,

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.959
who went to Oxford
and used to be a Democrat,

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.394
but has since adopted
the voice and mannerisms

00:05:29.394 --> 00:05:31.898
of a slow-talking,
suspender-wearing alligator

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.867
from a Disney movie
who threatens to drain the bayou

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.168
and replace it
with a shopping mall.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.237
"Well, what have we got here?

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.639
This swamp will make
a mighty fine Chick-Fil-A

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:43.575
if I do say so myself."

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:45.645
Honestly, you know
you've taken a real villain turn

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:49.848
when someone gasps off camera
and reacts to your line

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:52.251
of questioning the way soap
opera characters react

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.987
when an evil twin shows up.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.089
"Oh, my goodness, it's...

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:59.191
the evil John Kennedy."

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:01.294
[ Thunder booming ]

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.529
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.399
Worst part of my day today --

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:09.001
Wally -- the ol' cue card
Wally goes,

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.102
"Hey, are you going to be okay

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.570
remembering
the evil John Kennedy?

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.907
You need a second set of cards
over the other camera?"

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:16.642
I'm fine, bro.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.144
Crushed it.

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:20.580
-Yeah, you did good.
You did good.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:24.617
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.251
-And by the way,
a fellow senator,

00:06:26.251 --> 00:06:28.020
Democrat Tina Smith
of Minnesota,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.055
confirmed that it was her
who said,

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:32.591
"Oh, my goodness" off camera,
writing on Twitter,

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:34.593
"That person off camera is me

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:37.563
and what I was really thinking
was "holy [bleep]."

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:39.832
Which is appropriate
because the rest of Kennedy's

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.868
questions were also
holy [bleep].

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.470
For example,
earlier in that same exchange,

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.806
Kennedy asked her
if she had formally resigned

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.741
from a mandatory
school organization

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.809
in a country
that no longer exists.

00:06:50.809 --> 00:06:52.878
-You used to be a member
of a group

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:57.984
called the Young Communist,
didn't you?

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:04.957
-Senator, are you referring
to my membership

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:07.493
in the Youth
Communist Organization

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.728
while I was growing up
in the Soviet Union?

00:07:09.728 --> 00:07:13.132
-I don't know. I just wanted
to ask you that question.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:17.269
-Everybody in that country
was a member of the Komsomol,

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:20.172
which was the communist
youth organization.

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:22.407
-So you were -- were a member?

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:27.780
-That was a part of
normal progress in school.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.051
-Did you -- Have you resigned?
-From the...?

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.387
-From the Young Communists?

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:38.024
-You grow out of it with age
automatically.

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:41.794
-Did you -- Did you send them
a letter, though, resigning?

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:47.199
-Senator, this was many,
many years ago.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:49.968
As far as I remember
how the Soviet Union worked

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:51.804
was at a certain age,

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:54.573
you automatically stop
being a member.

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:56.008
-Could you look at your records

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:58.443
and see if you can find a copy?

00:07:58.443 --> 00:08:00.312
-I'm sorry.
Do you think schoolchildren

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:05.784
keep records that include copies
of letters they sent?

00:08:05.784 --> 00:08:08.287
If they did, I'd still
have all the letters I sent

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.857
Wendy Hughes asking her
what Aaron Matthews had

00:08:10.857 --> 00:08:14.494
that I didn't, and even worse,
I'd have copies of her response.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.732
But, sure, she should write
a formal letter of resignation

00:08:20.732 --> 00:08:22.134
to a country
that no longer exists.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.003
While she's doing that,
maybe you can write a letter

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:27.673
resigning from,
I don't know, Boss Hogg's gang?

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.675
This is what the unhinged
Republican Party is now.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.978
You can see the same
hysterical performance last week

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.980
from House GOP
leader Kevin McCarthy,

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:37.049
who staged a nearly nine-hour
meltdown on the House floor

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:38.584
over the Democrat's
social spending bill,

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:41.020
which, among other
radical socialist ideas,

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.855
provides funding
for universal pre-K,

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.357
extends the new child
tax credit mandates,

00:08:45.357 --> 00:08:47.259
paid family leave,
and expands Medicare

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:48.660
to include hearing aids.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.930
All that stuff is apparently
so unacceptable to McCarthy,

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.566
he lost his mind in a tantrum
that went past 5:00 a.m.

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:57.369
while being heckled by Democrats
from the back row.

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:59.705
-He delayed that vote
with a long,

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.874
very long, super long speech.

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:05.644
It lasted a record-breaking
eight hours and 32 minutes.

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:09.081
-This is the single most
reckless and irresponsible

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:12.117
spending bill
in our nation's history.

00:09:12.117 --> 00:09:16.188
I can look anywhere I want,
Mr. Speaker.

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:18.658
Mr. Speaker,
I cannot believe the amount

00:09:18.658 --> 00:09:20.592
of control one party rule wants.

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:23.061
They now want to dictate
to a member on the floor

00:09:23.061 --> 00:09:24.529
of where I can look?

00:09:24.529 --> 00:09:26.865
You ever eaten
one of these baby carrots?

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.267
I'll lead you
in a little secret.

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.668
There's no such thing.
They're just big carrots.

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.103
They chop them, they charge
you more, and you buy them.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.572
I have a friend
who serves in the Senate.

00:09:33.572 --> 00:09:36.108
Right before COVID,
he was on a [indistinct]

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:37.376
with other senators,

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.278
and he was sitting
and having a communication --

00:09:39.278 --> 00:09:41.847
maybe you've experienced
this as well --

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:47.519
with a military general
in the Chinese Communist Army.

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:50.589
You know what General
said to him?

00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:52.358
"America, you're weak."

00:09:52.358 --> 00:09:54.560
-McCarthy's got the amped-up
energy of a fifth grader

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.828
telling you about a classmate.

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:57.396
"I have a friend,
and his name is Timmy,

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:59.130
and he went to the zoo
and met a donkey

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:02.034
and the donkey took a big poop
and it was so funny."

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.571
Seriously, what was the point
of that story?

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:08.073
I feel like I zoned out during
an anecdote at a dinner party,

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:09.341
and now I have to catch up

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:10.642
to figure out what the hell
he's talking about.

00:10:10.642 --> 00:10:12.711
"Uh-huh? Oh, yeah.
Wow, so they kicked you out

00:10:12.711 --> 00:10:14.146
for having too many cats?"

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:18.183
"And now I have no one
to help me type up my lawsuits.

00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:20.753
They even took Klein."

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.588
Is this true about the baby
carrots

00:10:22.588 --> 00:10:24.256
are just big carrots
they cut up?

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:26.926
[ Laughter ]

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.299
What about baby corn?

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.438 --> 00:10:42.374
Seems like it should be
consistent

00:10:42.374 --> 00:10:45.310
across all the vegetables.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.845
[Bleep] hell of a way
to find out.

00:10:46.845 --> 00:10:48.948
That's all I'll say.

00:10:48.948 --> 00:10:51.550
The only fun anyone got out of
this demented spectacle

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.251
was getting the chance
to heckle McCarthy,

00:10:53.251 --> 00:10:55.287
like when Ohio
Congressman Tim Ryan

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:56.422
yelled at him from the back,

00:10:56.422 --> 00:10:57.723
"Keep going,
no one's listening."

00:10:57.723 --> 00:11:01.059
And then yesterday,
McCarthy went on to Fox News's

00:11:01.059 --> 00:11:03.061
most deranged shows
with Maria Bartiromo

00:11:03.061 --> 00:11:04.696
to be congratulated
for going off the deep end

00:11:04.696 --> 00:11:06.798
while whining about Democrats
interrupting him.

00:11:06.798 --> 00:11:08.234
-Congratulations.

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:12.505
How is your voice doing after
eight and a half hours speaking?

00:11:12.505 --> 00:11:13.939
-You know, my voice
is still strong

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:16.442
because it's still strong
for the American people.

00:11:16.442 --> 00:11:18.644
You know, when I went
to the floor,

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:21.246
I had no idea
we would speak that long.

00:11:21.246 --> 00:11:23.015
It wasn't about breaking
the record.

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:25.584
It was about
breaking down this bill

00:11:25.584 --> 00:11:28.087
and the amount of heckling
that they would try to do

00:11:28.087 --> 00:11:30.723
to stop me from
being able to talk.

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:32.925
-"I never thought I'd talk
that long,

00:11:32.925 --> 00:11:34.493
but right before
I went on the floor,

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:38.397
I got this very jarring news
about baby carrots."

00:11:38.397 --> 00:11:40.900
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.369 --> 00:11:45.504
This guy is such a goober.

00:11:45.504 --> 00:11:47.039
He sounds like
a substitute teacher

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:49.207
complaining to the principal
that his high school class

00:11:49.207 --> 00:11:51.343
won't stop chucking things
at him.

00:11:51.343 --> 00:11:53.979
"I got hit with
a spit ball, a paper airplane,

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:56.048
and fully knocked out
with a stapler.

00:11:56.048 --> 00:11:57.382
And then when I came to,
that changed

00:11:57.382 --> 00:12:00.619
my name of the chalkboard
to Mr. McFarty."

00:12:00.619 --> 00:12:02.254
Republican party
is just as unhinged

00:12:02.254 --> 00:12:04.190
as it was during the Trump
years, if not more so.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.557
They're fully devoted
to both Trump

00:12:05.557 --> 00:12:07.259
the man and the performance
of Trumpism,

00:12:07.259 --> 00:12:08.727
whether it's lying
about the election,

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:11.029
accusing people
of being secret communists,

00:12:11.029 --> 00:12:13.799
or staging deranged meltdowns
on the House floor.

00:12:13.799 --> 00:12:15.500
It reminds me
of something my very real

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.103
and totally not
imaginary friend once told me.

00:12:18.103 --> 00:12:19.338
He said, "Kevin McCarthy..."

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:20.639
-You're weak.

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:22.374
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:26.078
♪♪

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:27.279
God's Love We Deliver cooks

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:28.847
